{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,8]],"date-time":"2026-10-08T09:49:03Z","timestamp":1791452943469,"version":"4.3.3"},"reference-count":9,"publisher":"American Mathematical Society (AMS)","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Proc. Amer. Math. Soc."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1986,9]]},"abstract":"<p>\n                    \u010cencov has shown that Riemannian metrics which are derived from the Fisher information matrix are the only metrics which preserve inner products under certain probabilistically important mappings. In \u010cencov\u2019s theorem, the underlying differentiable manifold is the probability simplex\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"normal upper Sigma 1 Superscript n Baseline x Subscript i Baseline equals 1 comma x Subscript i Baseline greater-than 0\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msubsup>\n                              <mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\n                                \u03a3\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                              <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msubsup>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:msub>\n                                <mml:mi>x<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>i<\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msub>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>x<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>i<\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo>&gt;<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\Sigma _1^n{x_i} = 1, x_i &gt; 0<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    . For some purposes of using geometry to obtain insights about probability, it is more convenient to regard the simplex as a hypersurface in the positive cone. In the present paper \u010cencov\u2019s result is extended to the positive cone. The proof uses standard techniques of differential geometry but does not use the language of category theory.\n                  <\/p>","DOI":"10.1090\/s0002-9939-1986-0848890-5","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2010,7,11]],"date-time":"2010-07-11T16:16:50Z","timestamp":1278865010000},"page":"135-141","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["An extended \u010cencov characterization of the information metric"],"prefix":"10.1090","volume":"98","author":[{"given":"L. L.","family":"Campbell","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"14","reference":[{"key":"1","series-title":"Mathematics in Science and Engineering, Vol. 115","volume-title":"On measures of information and their characterizations","author":"Acz\u00e9l, J.","year":"1975"},{"issue":"2","key":"2","first-page":"357","article-title":"Differential geometry of curved exponential families\u2014curvatures and information loss","volume":"10","author":"Amari, Shun-ichi","year":"1982","journal-title":"Ann. Statist.","ISSN":"https:\/\/id.crossref.org\/issn\/0090-5364","issn-type":"print"},{"issue":"3","key":"3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"199","